        },
        "code": {
          "text": "Known right femoral hernia, small and reducible"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-1",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-1",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Mood and associated symptoms"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "For 3–4 weeks: low mood, feeling flat and teary, poor sleep with early waking, reduced appetite but still eating two meals daily, low energy while continuing housework, and anhedonia. Stopped the seniors exercise group because of worry that something bad will happen."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-2",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-2",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Health-related worries and checking behavior"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Marked worry about the femoral hernia, including repeated fears of strangulation or cancer and concern that cancer may have been missed. Googles the hernia and checks and pokes the area multiple times a day; this increases the ache."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-3",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-3",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Right groin discomfort and lump"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Mild intermittent right groin discomfort, worse with standing and settling with rest. Lump remains reducible when lying down."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-4",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-4",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Gastrointestinal and systemic symptoms"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Denies severe abdominal pain, constant pain, abdominal distension, nausea, vomiting, rectal bleeding, or fevers. Bowels are okay and passing wind."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-5",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-5",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Palpitations and associated symptoms"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Reports heart racing when reading online. Denies chest pain, shortness of breath, or presyncope."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-6",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-6",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Suicidal and self-harm thoughts"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Denies suicidal ideation and self-harm. States, “I don’t want to die, I’m just scared I might”. Future-focused, including talking about Christmas, seeing grandchildren, and the surgical appointment."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-7",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-7",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Phone examination and mental state"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Speaking in full sentences with no audible shortness of breath. Thoughts coherent; speech normal. Mood described as worried and low, with congruent affect and slight tremor in voice. No cognitive concerns in conversation."
      }
    },
    {
